  "verbalization": "Tatridin B appears to be a potential inhibitor of C8166 through a shared target, Ectonucleotide pyrophosphatase/phosphodiesterase family member 6, which is targeted by both Tatridin B and other compounds such as Aeruginosin DA722 and Paeonilactone C. This suggests that Tatridin B may exert its biological effects via a mechanism that involves the modulation of this enzyme, which is implicated in multiple cellular processes. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same pathway supports the hypothesis that Tatridin B may act through a similar mechanism, potentially influencing the same downstream pathways in C8166. The integrated evidence indicates a plausible, mechanistically linked relationship between Tatridin B and C8166, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action and therapeutic relevance.",
